2Bg6zNW7nvQ4544D0ThW8H2xKJ4q9fX5W5vpGfV8k2LBcW8jcf8F7vYT7mN5xVDWLThZK9W6FcR=
LV6gNlZrW1fRRkz8c9SBsW4RFZyv165dH_N6PGB7Bn7-jYW83NqJ38Y4jtnW2TGCFb3Wt0LvW2k=
JrRh8G2PppW7j0l8D96MQ0CW3d9rp57R169cW2hS-Pd6vWsqgVFlBkp5bjm0MW9j05Fn1KdyGfN=
4spw3K81JNYf6hvzvR04" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" style=
=3D"color:#192733" data-hs-link-id=3D"0" data-hs-link-id-v2=3D"Q4wxp1W+">fi=
rst used</a> by 14th-century Nahua people for dye and medicinal purposes.</=
p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">The plant=E2=80=99s brilliant red bracts =E2=
=80=94 which are leaves, not flowers =E2=80=94 were so revered by the Aztec=
 emperor Montezuma that thousands of them were transported to the high-alti=
tude capital of Tenochtitlan each winter.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">After Spain <a href=3D"https://media.hubspot.=
com/e3t/Ctc/UB+113/d2q-Vf04/VXdJJl2rPQ6rW7JK80z6p4Z2sVmLt1V5HkyHtN5wYXRY4Zw=
pbW7Y9pgv6lZ3pyW46pb1y8sCTCcW2LdyvB3kHTpWW5Kbddp3FPMhhW6FnH_h7yn3BBW6XsJzs7=
