 Dutch conglomerate in 2012.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">It marked the end of an era =E2=80=94 and the=
 beginning of a new, highly complex, international pipeline.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<h2 style=3D"margin:0; line-height:125%; font-size:18px"><strong>The modern=
 economics of poinsettias</strong></h2>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">Today, Ecke is owned by <strong>D=C3=BCmmen O=
range</strong>, one of the largest plant breeders in the world.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%"><strong>Rebecca Siemonsma</strong>, who worke=
d at Ecke from 2004-2012 and now oversees D=C3=BCmmen=E2=80=99s poinsettia =
operations, tells <em>The Hustle</em> that the company sells around <strong=
>50m </strong>of the plants each year =E2=80=94 more than half of the world=
=E2=80=99s supply.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">In other words, it=E2=80=99s likely that the =
poinsettias you see at your local Home Depot come from D=C3=BCmmen.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">The journey of a poinsettia plant looks somet=
hing like so:</p></div></div></td></tr></tbody></table>
