<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">Wenke Greenhouses is one of the 30 largest gr=
eenhouse operations in the US, with several million square feet of crops in=
 Michigan and Georgia.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">The company started growing poinsettias in th=
e mid-=E2=80=9980s. Today, it produces <strong>~200k</strong> annually, whi=
ch are sold wholesale to Walmart, Lowes, churches, and fundraisers.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">=E2=80=9CWe=E2=80=99ve had 2 great years,=E2=
=80=9D says <strong>Lorence Wenke</strong>, the company=E2=80=99s long-time=
 owner, who recently passed the business on to his daughter. =E2=80=9CPeopl=
e are staying indoors and plants are thriving across the board.=E2=80=9D</p=
>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%"><strong>Kevin Koeppler</strong> is the genera=
l manager at Sunbelt Greenhouses, a subsidiary of Wenke Greenhouses based i=
n Douglas, Georgia, where the poinsettias are grown.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">In a large spreadsheet shared with <em>The Hu=
stle</em>, he broke down what the poinsettia sector of the business looks l=
